      "writtenOn": "2024-04-03T21:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I am not convinced this is the best API shape for long term.\n\nIf we\u0027re not shipping the API in this form, can we just mark them as @hide and use constants from NPMS for now? (I don\u0027t know whether Flag allows rolling API back before finalization or not).\n\nI think we can write better APIs by having cleaner separation between \"metered\" restrictions, and NPMS can simply adopt them when they are available.\n\nOnce a SystemAPI is released, we have to support it for a really long time.",
      "revId": "37daa934593e9b43c25de86bce41784e64e7053d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
